# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the real file.
# The server reads these; they are never sent to the browser (§11, §20).

# ── Running on your own machine: put the keys here ──────────────────────────
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Running in a Claude Code cloud environment ──────────────────────────────
# Store each key there as an "API credential" rather than an environment
# variable — that dialog says plainly that environment variables are visible to
# anyone using the environment. An API credential is injected as a header by
# the egress proxy and never reaches this process, so there is no key to
# detect. Say so explicitly instead:
#
#   OPENAI_VIA_CREDENTIAL=1
#   ANTHROPIC_VIA_CREDENTIAL=1
#
# The credential's allowed website and header must match the provider:
#   OpenAI     api.openai.com      Authorization: Bearer <key>
#   Anthropic  api.anthropic.com   x-api-key: <key>       (no Bearer prefix)

# Optional overrides
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.5   # run 'npm run doctor' to see what your key actually has
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# PORT=3000
